<title>USA: US banks free reserves $899 mln/day Feb 26 two wks.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $899 mln/day Feb 26 two wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $899 million per day in the two weeks ended February 26, versus revised free reserves of $998 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $23 million, versus $18 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
